chat_history.turn:
Team of 3. Andrew owns the data core; Teammate A owns backend/analytics; Teammate B owns
frontend. To work independently, spend the first 60-90 minutes fixing three contracts:
DB schema, API contract (stub routes with example JSON), and mock data in /fixtures.

Teammate A timeline: 2-5 skeleton + stubs on Fly; 5-10 /predict and /opening-soon; 10-15
/recommend with PostGIS; 15-18 /demo/scenario; 18-22 tests, caching, load check.
Teammate B timeline: 2-5 scaffold + Vercel + map from fixtures; 5-10 live map on mocks;
10-14 Plan a visit against stubs; 14-18 Insights + swap to live API/Realtime; 18-22
mobile layout, demo panel, polish.
Andrew: 2-8 PostGIS zones, simulator, views + pg_cron; 8-14 Realtime, help integrate;
14-22 event scenarios, end-to-end testing, slides, backup demo; merge captain.

GitHub: monorepo with folder ownership; main always deployable; short lane-named branches;
PRs every 1-3 hours; squash merge; pull main before PR; CI required, reviews not required;
Actions with path filters; Vercel previews; Fly deploy on merge; Supabase CLI migrations;
Issues from Kiro tasks + Projects board; secrets never committed; tags v0.1-mvp and
v1.0-demo; syncs at hours 6, 10, 14, 18.
